{
  "version": 1,
  "id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000111",
  "title": "Particle System",
  "created_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "shared_cargo_toml": "[dependencies]\nplotters = \"0.3\"\n\n[profile.release]\nopt-level = 1\nlto = false\ncodegen-units = 16",
  "shared_source": "// \u2500\u2500 Deterministic PRNG (xorshift64) \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\npub struct Rng(pub u64);\n\nimpl Rng {\n    pub fn next_u64(&mut self) -> u64 {\n        self.0 ^= self.0 << 13;\n        self.0 ^= self.0 >> 7;\n        self.0 ^= self.0 << 17;\n        self.0\n    }\n\n    pub fn next_f64(&mut self) -> f64 {\n        (self.next_u64() as f64) / (u64::MAX as f64)\n    }\n\n    pub fn range(&mut self, lo: f64, hi: f64) -> f64 {\n        lo + self.next_f64() * (hi - lo)\n    }\n}\n\n// \u2500\u2500 Particle Simulation \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\nstruct Particle {\n    x: f64,\n    y: f64,\n    vx: f64,\n    vy: f64,\n    life: f64,\n    max_life: f64,\n}\n\n/// Simulates a particle fountain and returns snapshots at regular intervals.\n/// Each snapshot is a Vec of (x, y, life_fraction, speed) tuples.\npub fn simulate(\n    seed: u64,\n    total_steps: usize,\n    spawn_rate: usize,\n    gravity: f64,\n    snapshot_count: usize,\n) -> Vec<Vec<(f64, f64, f64, f64)>> {\n    let mut rng = Rng(seed);\n    let mut particles: Vec<Particle> = Vec::new();\n    let mut snapshots = Vec::with_capacity(snapshot_count);\n    let interval = total_steps / snapshot_count;\n\n    for step in 0..total_steps {\n        // Spawn new particles at the emitter\n        for _ in 0..spawn_rate {\n            let angle = rng.range(-0.5, 0.5);\n            let speed = rng.range(0.3, 0.7);\n            let max_life = rng.range(80.0, 160.0);\n            particles.push(Particle {\n                x: 0.0,\n                y: 0.0,\n                vx: angle * speed,\n                vy: speed,\n                life: max_life,\n                max_life,\n            });\n        }\n\n        // Physics update\n        for p in &mut particles {\n            p.x += p.vx;\n            p.y += p.vy;\n            p.vy += gravity;\n            p.life -= 1.0;\n        }\n\n        // Remove dead particles\n        particles.retain(|p| p.life > 0.0);\n\n        // Capture snapshot\n        if interval > 0 && (step % interval == 0 || step == total_steps - 1) {\n            snapshots.push(\n                particles\n                    .iter()\n                    .map(|p| {\n                        (\n                            p.x,\n                            p.y,\n                            (p.life / p.max_life).clamp(0.0, 1.0),\n                            (p.vx * p.vx + p.vy * p.vy).sqrt(),\n                        )\n                    })\n                    .collect(),\n            );\n        }\n    }\n\n    snapshots\n}\n",
  "cells": [
    {
      "id": "cell_0",
      "order": 0,
      "label": "Introduction",
      "cell_type": "Markdown",
      "source": "# Particle System \ud83c\udf86\n\nA **particle system** simulates many small, independent entities \u2014 *particles* \u2014 to create effects like fire, smoke, fountains, explosions, and rain.\n\n## How It Works\n\nEach particle has:\n- **Position** `(x, y)` \u2014 where it is\n- **Velocity** `(vx, vy)` \u2014 how it's moving\n- **Lifetime** \u2014 how long before it fades away\n\nEvery simulation step:\n1. **Spawn** new particles at the emitter with randomized velocities\n2. **Update** each particle: apply velocity to position, apply gravity to velocity\n3. **Age** each particle and remove dead ones\n\nThe result is an organic, flowing motion created from thousands of simple rules.\n\n## This Demo\n\nWe simulate a **fountain** \u2014 particles shoot upward from a central emitter, arc through gravity, and fade as they age. Color and size encode the particle's remaining life.",
      "cargo_toml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_1",
      "order": 1,
      "label": "Simulate",
      "cell_type": "Code",
      "source": "// Run the fountain simulation and display a summary.\nlet snapshots = shared::simulate(42, 300, 6, -0.003, 20);\n\nlet final_count = snapshots.last().map_or(0, |s| s.len());\nCellOutput::text(format!(\n    \"Simulation complete: {} snapshots captured, {} particles in final frame\",\n    snapshots.len(),\n    final_count,\n))\n",
      "cargo_toml": "[package]\nname = \"cell_1\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\nedition = \"2021\"\n\n[lib]\ncrate-type = [\"cdylib\"]\n\n[dependencies]\nironpad-cell = \"0.1\"\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_2",
      "order": 2,
      "label": "Final Frame",
      "cell_type": "Code",
      "source": "use plotters::prelude::*;\n\n// Run the simulation and render the final frame as a colorful scatter plot.\nlet snapshots = shared::simulate(42, 300, 6, -0.003, 20);\nlet frame = snapshots.last().unwrap();\n\nlet mut svg_buf = String::new();\n{\n    let root = SVGBackend::with_string(&mut svg_buf, (700, 500)).into_drawing_area();\n    root.fill(&RGBColor(15, 15, 25)).unwrap();\n\n    let mut chart = ChartBuilder::on(&root)\n        .caption(\n            \"Particle Fountain \u2014 Final Frame\",\n            (\"sans-serif\", 22).into_font().color(&WHITE),\n        )\n        .margin(15)\n        .x_label_area_size(30)\n        .y_label_area_size(40)\n        .build_cartesian_2d(-50.0_f64..50.0_f64, -10.0_f64..80.0_f64)\n        .unwrap();\n\n    chart\n        .configure_mesh()\n        .disable_mesh()\n        .axis_style(WHITE.mix(0.3))\n        .label_style((\"sans-serif\", 12).into_font().color(&WHITE.mix(0.5)))\n        .draw()\n        .unwrap();\n\n    // Each particle colored by remaining lifetime: bright cyan \u2192 dim red\n    chart\n        .draw_series(frame.iter().map(|&(x, y, life, _speed)| {\n            let r = (255.0 * (1.0 - life * 0.5)) as u8;\n            let g = (200.0 * life) as u8;\n            let b = (255.0 * life) as u8;\n            let size = 2 + (life * 4.0) as i32;\n            Circle::new((x, y), size, RGBColor(r, g, b).mix(life as f64).filled())\n        }))\n        .unwrap();\n\n    root.present().unwrap();\n}\n\nSvg(svg_buf)\n",
      "cargo_toml": "[package]\nname = \"cell_2\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\nedition = \"2021\"\n\n[lib]\ncrate-type = [\"cdylib\"]\n\n[dependencies]\nironpad-cell = \"0.1\"\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_3",
      "order": 3,
      "label": "Filmstrip",
      "cell_type": "Code",
      "source": "use plotters::prelude::*;\n\n// Render a 2\u00d72 filmstrip showing the fountain evolving over time.\nlet snapshots = shared::simulate(42, 300, 6, -0.003, 20);\nlet total = snapshots.len();\nlet indices = [0, total / 3, 2 * total / 3, total - 1];\n\nlet mut svg_buf = String::new();\n{\n    let root = SVGBackend::with_string(&mut svg_buf, (800, 600)).into_drawing_area();\n    root.fill(&RGBColor(15, 15, 25)).unwrap();\n\n    let panels = root.split_evenly((2, 2));\n\n    for (panel_idx, &frame_idx) in indices.iter().enumerate() {\n        let frame = &snapshots[frame_idx];\n        let panel = &panels[panel_idx];\n\n        let mut chart = ChartBuilder::on(panel)\n            .caption(\n                format!(\"Frame {}\", frame_idx + 1),\n                (\"sans-serif\", 16).into_font().color(&WHITE),\n            )\n            .margin(8)\n            .x_label_area_size(20)\n            .y_label_area_size(30)\n            .build_cartesian_2d(-50.0_f64..50.0_f64, -10.0_f64..80.0_f64)\n            .unwrap();\n\n        chart\n            .configure_mesh()\n            .disable_mesh()\n            .axis_style(WHITE.mix(0.2))\n            .label_style((\"sans-serif\", 10).into_font().color(&WHITE.mix(0.4)))\n            .draw()\n            .unwrap();\n\n        chart\n            .draw_series(frame.iter().map(|&(x, y, life, _)| {\n                let r = (255.0 * (1.0 - life * 0.5)) as u8;\n                let g = (200.0 * life) as u8;\n                let b = (255.0 * life) as u8;\n                let size = 2 + (life * 3.0) as i32;\n                Circle::new((x, y), size, RGBColor(r, g, b).mix(life as f64).filled())\n            }))\n            .unwrap();\n    }\n\n    root.present().unwrap();\n}\n\nSvg(svg_buf)\n",
      "cargo_toml": "[package]\nname = \"cell_3\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\nedition = \"2021\"\n\n[lib]\ncrate-type = [\"cdylib\"]\n\n[dependencies]\nironpad-cell = \"0.1\"\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_4",
      "order": 4,
      "label": "Variations",
      "cell_type": "Markdown",
      "source": "## Variations & Applications\n\n### Tweak the Parameters\n- **Gravity**: set to `0.0` for zero-G particles, or positive for rain falling down\n- **Spawn rate**: more particles per step \u2192 denser fountain\n- **Lifetime**: longer life \u2192 taller arcs and more particles alive at once\n- **Initial velocity**: wider angle range \u2192 broader spray\n\n### Other Effects\n- **Explosion**: spawn all particles at once with random velocities in all directions\n- **Fire**: particles drift upward with slight randomness, color gradient from yellow \u2192 orange \u2192 red \u2192 transparent\n- **Trail / comet**: spawn particles at a moving emitter, short lifetime\n\n### Why Rust + WASM?\nParticle systems benefit from raw throughput \u2014 updating thousands of particles per frame. Rust compiled to WASM gives near-native performance right in the browser, making this kind of simulation buttery smooth.",
      "cargo_toml": null
    }
  ]
}
